Ported files, with the Babylon.js source each came from and its version:

  animations/animator_avatar.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Animations/animatorAvatar.ts
    (AnimatorAvatar.retargetAnimationGroup, _retargetAnimationKeys),
    Babylon.js 9.31.2: carrying a clip's keys from one rig's rest onto
    another's, as SHAG retargets the shared player clips to each body.

  maths/math_glam.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Maths/math.vector.ts (Matrix.decompose,
    Quaternion.FromRotationMatrixToRef, FromUnitVectorsToRef,
    RotationQuaternionFromAxisToRef, RotationAxisToRef), Babylon.js 9.31.2:
    the helpers SHAG's player model fitting and held weapons call.

  maths/math_vector.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Maths/math.vector.ts (Vector3), Babylon.js 9.31.2:
    the arithmetic of add, subtract, scale, dot, cross, length, normalize and
    distance, kept in Babylon's operation order.

  materials/texture.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Materials/Textures/texture.ts (Texture),
    Babylon.js 9.31.2: getTextureMatrix and _prepareRowForTextureGeneration,
    for the default rotation centre and a rotation about W.

  materials/standard_material.rs, materials/standard.wgsl
    from packages/dev/core/src/Materials/standardMaterial.ts and
    fresnelParameters.ts, and the shaders default.vertex.fx,
    default.fragment.fx, ShadersInclude/lightsFragmentFunctions.fx,
    fresnelFunction.fx and defaultFragmentAlpha.fx, Babylon.js 9.31.2: the
    StandardMaterial terms SHAG's procedural pickups use (hemispheric and
    directional diffuse and specular, emissive colour and texture, emissive
    and opacity Fresnel, diffuse alpha, RGB opacity, ambient, emissive as
    illumination, texture matrix and level, alpha modes and image processing
    contrast), rewritten in WGSL.

  meshes/vertex_data.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Meshes/mesh.vertexData.ts (ComputeNormals,
    transform, merge) and mesh.ts (MergeMeshes, bakeTransformIntoVertices,
    convertToFlatShadedMesh), Babylon.js 9.31.2.

  meshes/mesh_builder.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Meshes/Builders/boxBuilder.ts,
    sphereBuilder.ts, torusBuilder.ts, cylinderBuilder.ts and
    planeBuilder.ts, Babylon.js 9.31.2: the vertex data for the options
    SHAG's procedural pickups pass.

  meshes/ico_sphere_builder.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Meshes/Builders/icoSphereBuilder.ts
    (CreateIcoSphereVertexData), Babylon.js 9.31.2: positions and indices,
    as SHAG's explosion fireball takes them.

  meshes/ribbon_builder.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Meshes/Builders/ribbonBuilder.ts
    (CreateRibbonVertexData) and mesh.vertexData.ts (_ComputeSides),
    Babylon.js 9.31.2: two open paths, double sided, as SHAG's projectile
    trails build them.

  post_processes/image_processing_post_process.rs, post_processes/image_processing.wgsl
    from packages/dev/core/src/Materials/imageProcessingConfiguration.ts,
    PostProcesses/imageProcessingPostProcess.ts and the shaders
    imageProcessing.fragment.fx, ShadersInclude/imageProcessingFunctions.fx
    and helperFunctions.fx, Babylon.js 9.31.2: exposure, the vignette, gamma
    and contrast from an HDR target, rewritten in WGSL.

  post_processes/fxaa_post_process.rs, post_processes/fxaa.wgsl
    from packages/dev/core/src/PostProcesses/fxaaPostProcess.ts,
    thinFXAAPostProcess.ts and the shaders ShadersWGSL/fxaa.vertex.fx and
    fxaa.fragment.fx, Babylon.js 9.31.2: FXAA over the final image.

  meshes/trail_mesh.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Meshes/trailMesh.ts (TrailMesh), Babylon.js
    9.31.2: the tube of rings and its per-frame update, as SHAG's ragdolls
    trail one behind the hips.

  physics/v2/ragdoll.rs
    from packages/dev/core/src/Physics/v2/ragdoll.ts (Ragdoll), Babylon.js
    9.31.2: the boxes, their joints and the bone sync, on rapier3d bodies
    in place of Havok aggregates.
